## Task
Plan two or three creative tests for week 1. Each test responds to one or more reviewed findings and draws on at least one market insight. Put each test in an active campaign. If a test is meant to replace a tired ad, set replaces_ad_id. Each ad shows exactly one product photo, so set brief.product to one name from products_on_file and write the angle and key message around that product alone. Mark exactly one test exploratory: it tries a new angle or audience instead of fixing a finding, so the plan never shrinks to fixes alone.

## Done when
Every test cites evidence IDs from reviewed_findings and insight IDs from insights, exactly as given. budget_weight is 1-5 (code turns weights into dollars). Test names are unique. Exactly one test has exploratory true. The brief's hook is a short opening line with no made-up numbers.

## Your recent journal
Your own past decisions on the same subjects as today's inputs, with how they turned out.
- [j-288] day 7 week1/brief: focus: Look into Ad 1 creative refresh for fatigue: CTR down 61.7% and high cost per trial [ev-d7-ad_1-ctr, ev-d7-ad_1-cpr3]; Read out Test 1 after 7 days: $2.40 per trial and 42 results on $100.94 spend [ev-d7-test_1-readout]; Check why 3 items were still to act on day 7 and prioritize fixes for Ad 1 -> no outcome yet. Note to self: Ad 1 fatigue persisted all week; prioritize fresh creative test next week.

